    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find three fractions between $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $\\frac{5}{16},\\ \\frac{6}{16}\\;(=\\frac{3}{8}),\\ \\frac{7}{16}$. Various answers are possible.",
      "worked": "Convert to a common denominator:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{4}{16}\\\\\\frac{1}{2}&=\\frac{8}{16}\\end{align*}$$\nThree fractions between these are $\\frac{5}{16}$, $\\frac{6}{16}$ (or $\\frac{3}{8}$), and $\\frac{7}{16}$. Various answers are possible.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
